A||||11||GTMike||how to spot a turbo MR2 from a NA MR2???||||1||
Z||000000||GTMike||12-07-2001||02:33 AM||||how do you tell the diff,  looking at the car from outside.   i want to know so i dont race a turbo on accident. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||reddog||12-07-2001||02:51 AM||||except for the turbo tag on the right rear of the decklid. You can't tell the difference. I used to have one.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||artherd||12-07-2001||04:09 AM||||If you hear blow-off valves, slam into reverse and run away!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Seriously, asside from the little 'turbo' insignia, and the 1" larger rear wheels, there's almost no way to tell untill you loose  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Race anyway, it's fun, and you may meet a mid-engine enthusiest!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000003||mrfiero||12-07-2001||03:01 PM||||On the decklid.....look for the raised grilles.  The turbo (and first gen supercharged) MR2's have raised grilles, the NA models are flush with  the decklid.<P>Also, most (not all) '91-'95 turbo models have front driving/fog lights.<P>Another clue is roof type.......if it has a sunroof or hard top then it is NA.......all turbos (and some NA's) have T-Tops.<P>The final "clue" is on the right hand corner of the rear decklid......there is a "turbo" badge that is color coded to the rest of the car.  It's kind of stealthy, but it's there.<P>The biggest clue, however, is the raised decklid grilles......only the turbo models got these.<P>I guess there is one more clue......if the MR2 is pulling away from your V-6 Fiero then it is the turbo model.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  A V-6 Fiero should easily outpace an NA MR2.<P>Happy hunting!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   ||||reg||1
Z||000004||btoth||12-07-2001||04:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>The biggest clue, however, is the raised decklid grilles......only the turbo models got these.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yep!||||reg||14
Z||000005||AusFiero||12-07-2001||04:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by btoth:<BR><B> Yep!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Yep here too. Thats the easiest way. But you do know a normally aspirated MR2 has more power than a standard Fiero V6 right?<P>Fiero V6 140hp - 2nd Gen MR2 157hp (Well the Australian model has. I am just assuming America has the same model.) Turbo 2nd Gen MR2 225hp<BR><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero3.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000006||Smokin' GT||12-07-2001||05:01 PM||||Someone correct me if I'm wrong but I believe the U.S. 2nd gen. N/A MR2's are only 130 horses while the turbo's are 190<P>------------------<BR>-87 Bright Blue Metallic GT-<BR>          -Joel||||reg||4
Z||000007||mrfiero||12-07-2001||11:30 PM||||Unfortunately for us here in the states we get the "wimpy" versions of European & Japanese cars.  The US spec '91-'95 NA MR2's had/has 140HP and the turbo is an even 200 (200 horses & 200 pounds of torque).<P>Horsepower on the NA may be the same as the Fiero, but the Fieros torque pushes it ahead.  We have no chance (stock vs. stock) against a turbo model.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Way back in 1990 I almost traded in my '88 GT on a brand new MR2 turbo.....the test drive was incredible.  I scared the $hit out of the salesman.......we were doing 90MPH on the onramp to the freeway and I was still accelerating.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I think I would have had more ticket issues than I wound up with over the oast 11+ years if I had bought it (I got into enough trouble with the Fiero!).  <P>Actually, the main reason I didn't buy it was cost.  I paid $9000 for my '88 GT in April 1990 (with 24K miles) and a new loaded MR2 turbo was over $20K.....I just couldn't afford it.   <P>Oh well.||||reg||1
Z||000008||MR2KLR||12-08-2001||12:21 AM||||Yes yes yes!!! if it is a newer (90+) you will plainly see the "Turbo" badge ON THE BACK left of the deck lid. and if it's N/A you will see the lack of fog lights up FRONT if you know what I mean  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> you'll see the grilles from the back too.<P>------------------<BR>  <BR>Black 88 Coupe: 120 MPH spedo, Aux. gauge pod, 195/55VR14 Potenza RE-71 tires, GT exhaust & ground F/X Soon to have 16" White Beretta GTZ W/ 215/45ZR16's<BR><A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOY/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's Page</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||FieroMaster88||12-08-2001||01:45 AM||||Yes....Turbo badge on the back.  I didnt know this white MR2 at school was TURBO until I was behind it at a light and noticed the TURBO badge.  It was painted the same color as the body!||||reg||1
Z||000010||AusFiero||12-08-2001||02:37 AM||||Hmm so Australia does get better models than America then. My MR2 is a normally aspirated GT and leaves the Fiero for dead in all respects. Well except looks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I have since added a custom exhaust and cold air intake to the MR2 and it gets along quite well. May add some cams and a new chip to push it along a little better again. I was going to fit a turbo engine but it just wasn't worth the hassle insurance wise.<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero3.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000011||btoth||12-08-2001||11:33 AM||||I know a lot of the "hardcore" MR2 people put J-spec engines in their cars because of the significant power increase.  (Doesn't it have to do with all of our stupid emissions regulations??)<P>My friend has a '91 N/A 5-speed, and versus my '86 GT auto neither one of us could pull away from the other... but that was only up to the next red-light, so that's not a very good measure of anything.  I could've sworn that his only has 120hp and 130ft lbs of torque.  But I may be wrong... I'll ask.<p>[This message has been edited by btoth (edited 12-08-2001).]||||reg||1
